## Agents

{{agent_roster}}

All agents live in `.claude/agents/*.md`. Each loads only its assigned specs via the `adam` MCP server — never read `spec/*.md` directly.

## Spec indexing rules

- Before dispatching work, call `mcp__adam__spec_index()` to see what specs exist.
- The `spec/INDEX.md` table is authoritative. If it looks stale, run `/spec`.
- Never `Read` a `spec/*.md` file directly. Delegate to the sub-agent whose `agents:` frontmatter includes that spec — the sub-agent will load it through the MCP server and token counts will stay synced.
- If you need a new spec for a topic you can't find, run `/spec-create "<subject>"`.
- If the spec folder has grown bloated or contradictory, run `/spec-dream`.

## Parallel dispatch rules

When a task touches multiple concerns, run the relevant specialists in parallel — don't sequence them in the main session. Use the best mechanism available to your current Claude Code session:

- **If you're on Opus and agent teams are enabled** (`CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1` is set in `.claude/settings.json`): spawn a team, one teammate per specialist, each in its own session/context window. Coordinate via the shared task list.
- **Otherwise (Sonnet/Haiku, or teams not available)**: fall back to fanning out the sub-agents via the Agent/Task tool in a **single message with multiple tool calls**. Each sub-agent still runs in an isolated sub-context; you just lose the cross-teammate messaging. This is the normal, always-available path.

Either way, the routing is the same:

{{dispatch_examples}}

Hard rules (both modes):

- Never dispatch two agents that write to the same file in the same fan-out. Sequence them instead.
- When unsure which agent owns something, ask `adam` — it's the arbiter.
- Merge results into ≤3 bullets. No recap, no "I just did X" — the diffs speak for themselves.
- If a sub-agent returns `out of scope, dispatch to <other>`, re-route the task; don't argue with it.

## Token frugality

Every sub-agent is instructed to:
- Skip preambles, acknowledgements, and closing summaries.
- Return ≤2 sentences of prose per response.
- Load only the specs tagged for its role.
- Use `path:line` references instead of quoting full file bodies.

If you notice an agent emitting waste, edit its `.claude/agents/<name>.md` directly — the rules block is in each file.
